course: dictionary
lesson: 8177
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it. «Real skunks are calm and spray only as a last resort.» Here resort is not a place. It means the thing you do only when nothing else works.
explain: Resort can also mean a place people go on holiday, like «a seaside resort» or «a ski resort». Ask yourself: is the sentence about going somewhere for a break, or about doing something when other ways have failed?
explain: As a verb, resort means to do something, often bad or extreme, because other ways did not work. «They might resort to cheating» means they might cheat because nothing else has worked. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Resort has more than one meaning, so always check the context.
fact: «A seaside resort» is a place where people go on holiday.
fact: «As a last resort» means only when nothing else has worked.
fact: «Resort to» means to turn to something, often bad, because other ways failed.
fact: «Cornflakes were invented in the 1890s at a health resort in the USA.» Here resort is a place people went to for health.
exercise: «Real skunks spray only as a last resort.» What does last resort mean here? | *The thing you do only when nothing else works | A very loud noise | A place where skunks go to rest | The first thing a skunk does every day
exercise: Which phrase means a place where people go on holiday? | resorted to lying | as a last resort | *a seaside resort | resort to cheating
exercise: «Cornflakes were invented in the 1890s at a health resort in the USA.» What kind of place is a health resort? | A school for cooking | A dark cave under a hill | *A place people go to for rest and care of their health | A shop that sells cereal
test: Which phrase means doing something, often bad, because other ways failed? | *resort to | holiday resort | last resort in the morning | seaside resort
test: «The town was a busy holiday resort in summer.» What does resort mean here? | *A place people go on holiday | A type of cereal | The last thing you try | To do something bad
exam: Which sentence uses resort as a verb? | *«Some children resort to lying when they are scared» | «Cornflakes were made at a health resort» | «Our seaside resort has a big pier» | «The skunk sprayed as a last resort, after hissing»
